{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_recurrence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_recurrence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_recurrence.lean#L81-L92","doc":"**Lepton continuant recurrence theorem.** Bundles the Morgan–\nVoyce recurrence into a single conjunction: for every `n`, the\nsequences `a_n` and `b_n` jointly satisfy the four characterising\nrelations of `prop:lepton-continuant-recurrence`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:lepton-continuant-recurrence","label":"prop:lepton-continuant-recurrence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/lepton-continuant-recurrence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.netCoeff_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.netCoeff_succ","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_recurrence.lean#L72-L79","doc":"**Net-coefficient identity**: `net_{n+1} = b_n + b_{n+1}`.\n\nDischarged by unfolding `netCoeff`, `morganVoyceA`, and applying\n`morganVoyceA_succ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceA_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceA_succ","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_recurrence.lean#L66-L70","doc":"**a_n = b_{n−1}** identity, packaging the first equation of the\nMorgan–Voyce recurrence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_recurrence.lean#L56-L64","doc":"**Recurrence identity** for `b_n` ([`prop:lepton-continuant-recurrence`]).\n\nHolds by definition: this is the second equation of the Morgan–\nVoyce recurrence packaged as a Lean theorem so downstream\nconsumers can `rw` against it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.netCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.netCoeff","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_recurrence.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The \"net coefficient\" of `T_{2,n} = σ₀ⁿ` is `a_n + b_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceA","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_recurrence.lean#L46-L50","doc":"The companion sequence `a_n = b_{n-1}` (with `a_0 = 0`), so that\nthe NF decomposition `σ₀ⁿ = a_n + b_n · σ₀` holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_recurrence.lean#L37-L44","doc":"The Morgan–Voyce continuant `b_n` defined by\n`b_0 = 0`, `b_1 = 1`, `b_{n+2} = X · b_{n+1} + b_n`\nover `Polynomial ℤ`.  The coefficient symbol `X` plays the role\nof the Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}